      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if the host never issues the __pkvm__vcpu_after_set_cpuid hypercall? Do we still ensure we enable x2APIC in such case?\n\nIf not, it seems we should call kvm_apic_set_base() when creating the protected vCPU instead (e.g. after calling kvm_vcpu_reset() in __vcpu_create(), to override the xAPIC setting done by kvm_lapic_reset())? And then here we can e.g. just check guest_cpu_cap_has(vcpu, X86_FEATURE_X2APIC), instead of calling kvm_apic_set_base() again?\n\nBTW also I\u0027m wondering: is there any easy way to check if x2APIC is enabled in the `new` CPUID _before_ calling `kvm_set_cpuid(vcpu, new, new_nent)` to set this CPUID (so that we don\u0027t need to switch back to the old CPUID after that if the check fails)?",
      "revId": "863f921b11605d0568635b675b4dea50b7c52825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
